  activeSettings:
    name: Paid
    id: 30c0eca9-01de-41b5-bf2e-1a8e9a1206f7
    skin: Custom
    fileName: Paid
    redistributable: 0
    lite: 0
    priority: 5
    type: json
  allSettings:
  - name: Default
    id: d7524b26-de72-4395-9067-cdd6631042ca
    skin: Default
    fileName: Default
    redistributable: 0
    lite: 1
    priority: 7
    type: json
  - name: Paid
    id: 30c0eca9-01de-41b5-bf2e-1a8e9a1206f7
    skin: Custom
    fileName: Paid
    redistributable: 0
    lite: 0
    priority: 5
    type: json
  readmeData:
    richText: 'Greetings!


      We are pushing the 3D platformer controller a bit
      more here as well as addressing a few issues that Level 2 still had.


      Here
      is a list of new features:

      -we now check that we are moving in a direction
      before rotating the character

      -the jump has been fine tuned

      -we
      are using a model and are animating it

      -it''s not a state machine just
      yet but we are using a few variables in the script to know when we can jump
      and such


      To look at the way the animator works go to Window > Animation
      > Animator while seleting the prefab "Edward"

      This is the place that
      manages all the animations I''m using. You can look at the platformer script
      to see what kind of methods I use to communicate with the animator.

'
    textAreaObjectFields: []
    objectIdPairs: []
